    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Riskified is riding a wave of strong operational momentum as ecommerce fraud grows more complex, reinforcing demand for its risk intelligence platform. The quarter featured record volumes and broad-based gains from new merchant wins and AI-powered product launches, underscoring its expanding role in the global payments ecosystem. Gross merchandise volume surged, reflecting deeper engagement with existing clients and successful land-and-expand with blue-chip brands. While the macro backdrop is generally supportive, foreign-exchange swings present a notable headwind, and analyst opinion remains split, with at least one research firm still negative.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership reached a pivotal inflection point, delivering the company’s first-ever GAAP profit alongside notable margin expansion. The team is pairing this operational improvement with a confident 2026 outlook and an expanded share repurchase authorization, signaling conviction in the trajectory. Guidance acknowledges a material foreign-exchange drag, yet management expects continued growth and margin progress. This combination of reaching profitability, returning capital to shareholders, and setting achievable targets is beginning to repair credibility, though the lingering sell rating from one research provider shows the market is not yet fully convinced of the sustainability of the turnaround.",
